\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Refinement-matched external benchmark, $960$ shared-realization trials per SNR. Short legend labels denote the proposed MKSC-GI+CCOP-JVP, range-scaled 4-D Jones-VP, ALS-CPD with joint mapping, VBI/SBL with joint refinement, and near-field OMP--SAGE--WLS routes. Each column asks one question of position (top) and of the clock or its reconstruction (bottom): precision inside the basin, a tail-sensitive statistic, and the failure rate. (b)~p99 is the nearest-rank tenth-largest error of the cell, so it enters the wrong-basin population once that mass exceeds about $1\%$; the shaded region is the $0.1$-m inlier threshold. (d)~The CEB reference is the median bound of Section~\ref {subsec:res_setup} scaled by $\sigma $, since the benchmark suite logs no per-trial CEB. The dotted line in~(c) and~(f) is one trial in $960$, i.e. $0.104\%$, and hollow markers on that line are exact zeros. Unconditional RMSE and p95 are tabulated in the supplement. Continuous refiners converge similarly inside the correct basin; acquisition reliability separates their tails.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_combined}{{4}{13}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Serialized single-thread cost at $-10$~dB: one process, one BLAS thread, peak resident set size sampled every $10$~ms, $30$ trials per row.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cost}{{II}{13}{}{}{}}
